              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "marty"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for our office Christmas party and it was really good. I made half the recipe (one can of pineapple juice, about one little packet of the raspberry ice Crystal Light, and one liter bottle of soda). I used club soda instead of sugary soda. I thought the lemon-lime soda would make it too sweet. If you're making it for kids then go with the sweet soda. I'm making it again for Xmas Eve and will be spiking it with vodka or rum.",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-19T10:47:06.167Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SammyD122"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this punch for a bridal shower (and spiked it with Bacardi Rum!) and it was a total hit! Everyone was asking for the recipe! P.S. It definitely should be 0.4 oz package of drink mix (I used Crystal Lite), NOT 4 oz!",
            "datePublished": "2010-11-02T12:52:31.123Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mamcamij"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled this for a dinner get together and it went over well. For the soda-pop, I used Fresca, and it gave it just enough sweetness to the drink. It was perfect. Will most definitely use this recipe again! Loved it.",
            "datePublished": "2009-05-18T10:43:12.077Z"
